Z||000000||Formula88||08-20-2001||01:09 PM||||So, being the informed Pennock's member that I am, when I noticed my heater core appeared to be leaking, I did a search for heater core info.  What did I find?  200 posts of people telling other people to do a search on heater core info.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <P>Oh, well.  I finally did find some info, but I had to sift through a lot of crap first.<P>Has anyone else noticed this trend?  Everyone's so much in a hurry to tell people to do a search, there's more posts telling people to do a search than there are with useable info in them.  ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||08-20-2001||06:21 PM||||I agree completely. If you don't want to go to the trouble of typing out a big "how-to" replay, maybe jsut see if someone else wants to before you tell people to go search for it. After all this isn't the Fiero FAQ Search Engine. New info on things is brought up by people talking about old and common subjects. Allot of new ppl on this forum, im sure they all know things some of us don't.||||reg||2
Z||000002||Cheever3000||08-21-2001||10:53 PM||||Almost <B>ALL</B> of the real information I post (not the loonie stuff) was obtained by clicking that little "search" button and typing a few simple words.  I give people information, tips and guidance all the time, which they could have gotten themselves from the same place I got it.  If you got too much in your results, you didn't make the searches specific enough.  There's not a question about Fieros that can't be answered <B>quickly</B> by searching the Forum, and I'd bet money on it!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||08-21-2001||11:04 PM||||Since that last post (and I was interrupted by a phone call from my boss, and I had to type this post) I found over a dozen topics about heater core problems.  I read 9 of them, and not a single one included any advice to do a search.<P>(Editing to correct my choice of words, because it was over a dozen <I>topics</I>, not a dozen posts.  I read every post in each of the 9 topics that I opened.)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
